{
    "background_story": "Finnley was a majestic oak tree standing tall in the heart of the Whispering Woods. For centuries, he watched over the forest and its creatures, providing shade and shelter from the harshest of storms. As the seasons changed, Finnley's leaves would undergo a process of abscission, letting go of the old to make way for the new. It was a bittersweet time, as he bid farewell to the worn and weary leaves that had danced in the summer breeze. But with each autumn, Finnley's roots grew stronger, and his branches more resilient. He came to understand that abscission was not an end, but a necessary step towards renewal. As the wind whispered secrets through his leaves, Finnley stood as a testament to the cyclical nature of life, where letting go was a crucial part of growth and transformation.",
